    "resolution": {
      "title": "The Smoke-Pearl",
      "text": "A smoke-pearl. A lamp-diver's lamp guttered in a cistern of the Ribs; a mussel swallowed the flame and kept it, year after year, wrapped in black.\n\nSomeone carried it all the way down the Stair and hid it in a hollow book, “for safekeeping — not for the reliquary, not yet.” Not yet, as though they always meant it for the reliquary in the end.\n\nBrother Alder, when you tell him, goes and gets a pencil and draws something in the back of your journal: a coil of glass, a condenser, a stand. “A still,” he says. “Stillkeepers' still. If you're going to start opening things, you'll want to be able to take them apart properly.”",
      "payload": {}
    }
  }
